1
00:00:36,625 --> 00:00:38,458
We have one last chance.

2
00:00:38,958 --> 00:00:41,166
To do what?

3
00:00:41,666 --> 00:00:44,416
To rob the collection tonight.

4
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:48,583
Have you lost your mind?
Did you see what they have in there?

5
00:00:48,666 --> 00:00:51,958
Wire fences, jammers, fighting bulls…
This isn't the Paris heist.

6
00:00:52,041 --> 00:00:54,708
They shot Bruce
for setting foot on that estate.

7
00:00:54,791 --> 00:00:56,666
It's a miracle he and Keila survived.

8
00:00:56,750 --> 00:00:59,500
You're right. Paris is Paris.

9
00:01:00,333 --> 00:01:05,500
And this is Spain's underbelly.
We must rise to the challenge.

10
00:01:28,583 --> 00:01:29,708
Catch, Damián.

11
00:01:49,583 --> 00:01:52,500
So, shooting our way in is your only plan?

12
00:01:52,583 --> 00:01:53,416
You're wrong.

13
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:56,416
We'll go in through the door,
like we own the place.

14
00:01:56,500 --> 00:02:00,458
Here are the magnetic keys
to gain access to the estate.

15
00:02:04,541 --> 00:02:06,333
What do we do with that guy?

16
00:02:06,416 --> 00:02:09,083
You and Roi are going to stay
and watch him.

17
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:12,416
Since he's our guest.

18
00:02:12,916 --> 00:02:16,458
Pick the buckshot from his face
and disinfect his wounds

19
00:02:16,541 --> 00:02:19,666
so he can go home tomorrow good as new.

20
00:02:20,583 --> 00:02:25,000
I'm not a nurse, but I can drive
into the estate and haul ass right back.

21
00:02:25,083 --> 00:02:28,500
Jesus, Berlin, I think I can be
a lot more useful there than here.

22
00:02:28,583 --> 00:02:30,541
More than Bruce. No offense.

23
00:02:33,541 --> 00:02:36,708
Cameron, this isn't
for professional reasons but personal.

24
00:02:36,791 --> 00:02:38,083
I'm doing this for you.

25
00:02:40,208 --> 00:02:41,916
For your romantic reconciliation.

26
00:02:43,208 --> 00:02:47,041
Stay and watch this scoundrel.
You'll see how well it works out for you.

27
00:02:47,125 --> 00:02:51,875
Hand on the trigger, adrenaline, fear…

28
00:02:51,958 --> 00:02:54,333
That reinvigorates any couple.

29
00:02:59,291 --> 00:03:02,291
Or do any of you want
to apply to be leader of the crew?

30
00:03:43,083 --> 00:03:45,375
Hey, are you all right?

31
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,125
No, Bruce, I'm not.

32
00:03:50,625 --> 00:03:53,791
Earlier, in this same vehicle,
I thought you had been killed.

33
00:03:54,291 --> 00:03:57,416
Hey. In the end, nothing happened.

34
00:03:58,166 --> 00:03:59,416
All thanks to you.

35
00:04:00,791 --> 00:04:03,541
Racing in like Ayrton Senna.

36
00:04:19,125 --> 00:04:22,958
Bruce, before we go back in there,
I need to tell you something.

37
00:04:24,958 --> 00:04:28,125
I had doubts for a while.

38
00:04:32,750 --> 00:04:33,833
I had a…

39
00:04:35,208 --> 00:04:37,541
a moment of confusion with a guy.

40
00:04:38,291 --> 00:04:41,833
I only saw him once. It wasn't planned.
It didn't mean anything.

41
00:04:42,541 --> 00:04:45,208
What are you talking about, Keila?

42
00:04:45,291 --> 00:04:47,958
Kissing, being turned on, banging?

43
00:04:49,833 --> 00:04:51,916
- Yes.
- Yes to what, Keila?

44
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:56,166
It was sexual contact.
But just once. No repeats.

45
00:04:58,875 --> 00:05:02,750
When that man took you at gunpoint, I…

46
00:05:02,833 --> 00:05:06,750
I panicked. And I froze.

47
00:05:07,708 --> 00:05:10,125
When I thought
that I might not see you again,

48
00:05:11,083 --> 00:05:13,375
this overpowering force came over me.

49
00:05:13,458 --> 00:05:15,750
I pictured myself doing the unthinkable,

50
00:05:15,833 --> 00:05:17,541
running that man over.

51
00:05:18,041 --> 00:05:22,291
I swear, if he had done something to you,
I'd have bashed his head in with a stone.

52
00:05:23,333 --> 00:05:24,333
Bruce.

53
00:05:27,458 --> 00:05:29,375
You are the force that moves me.

54
00:05:38,416 --> 00:05:40,625
I know it hurts, but I had to tell you.

55
00:05:41,125 --> 00:05:42,291
Well, now you have.

56
00:05:45,041 --> 00:05:47,083
<i>We are approaching the entrance.</i>

57
00:05:48,958 --> 00:05:50,541
We're going in. Be ready.

58
00:06:19,583 --> 00:06:22,291
Thermal sensors
show no orange or red blobs.

59
00:06:22,375 --> 00:06:24,791
No one in a 30-meter radius.

60
00:06:26,208 --> 00:06:27,583
Turn off the lights.

61
00:06:47,083 --> 00:06:49,791
The electric fence is six meters ahead.

62
00:06:56,666 --> 00:06:58,416
<i>No heat sources. We can go in.</i>

63
00:07:15,583 --> 00:07:18,041
The air vent is three kilometers
to the northeast.

64
00:07:18,125 --> 00:07:19,875
Stick to this route, Damián.

65
00:07:26,958 --> 00:07:28,833
I see infrared radiation.

66
00:07:29,791 --> 00:07:32,166
- Where?
- Behind the bushes. On the left.

67
00:07:33,458 --> 00:07:35,208
Roll down your window.

68
00:07:36,666 --> 00:07:38,500
I can't see through the branches.

69
00:07:50,291 --> 00:07:52,291
There are a few of them now.

70
00:07:57,083 --> 00:07:59,083
We're being followed. Let's go.

71
00:07:59,791 --> 00:08:01,125
Wait.

72
00:08:07,333 --> 00:08:09,000
Bulls. Don't be hysterical.

73
00:08:13,875 --> 00:08:15,000
Kill that flashlight.

74
00:08:57,583 --> 00:09:01,250
You left marks on my face,
and no one messes with my face.

75
00:09:01,333 --> 00:09:05,083
Shut up. Save your energy
for hunting wild boars.

76
00:09:13,083 --> 00:09:16,250
Let her go, dammit!
Let her go, you bastard!

77
00:09:19,083 --> 00:09:21,208
Roi! No!

78
00:09:21,291 --> 00:09:23,083
- Let go of her, dammit!
- Shoot!

79
00:09:25,416 --> 00:09:26,916
Fucking shoot!

80
00:09:36,833 --> 00:09:38,375
Why didn't you shoot?

81
00:09:38,458 --> 00:09:40,708
I can't shoot a guy for biting your hair.

82
00:09:41,375 --> 00:09:43,625
He was gonna rip my face off, asshole!

83
00:09:44,625 --> 00:09:47,250
Berlin asked us to keep him alive.

84
00:09:47,333 --> 00:09:50,291
Know what Berlin would've done?
Pumped him full of lead.

85
00:09:50,791 --> 00:09:53,125
You're all bark and no bite. A lapdog.

86
00:09:53,208 --> 00:09:54,375
What I am is loyal.

87
00:09:54,458 --> 00:09:56,583
Something you wouldn't understand.

88
00:09:57,666 --> 00:10:02,166
What? Got nothing to say?
That's why you can't work with me.

89
00:10:03,250 --> 00:10:04,583
You're ashamed.

90
00:10:05,958 --> 00:10:08,458
You can't look me in the eye
after what you did.

91
00:10:13,166 --> 00:10:14,333
I warned you.

92
00:10:16,125 --> 00:10:20,000
- I told you who I am and what I can give.
- Did I put a gun to your head?

93
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,541
You did everything but.

94
00:10:22,625 --> 00:10:27,041
You got on your knees,
begging me to give us a try. Remember?

95
00:10:32,958 --> 00:10:36,041
You confused me. You messed with my head.

96
00:10:38,458 --> 00:10:40,958
Do you know why you ignored
everything I said?

97
00:10:42,541 --> 00:10:44,666
You're a fucking pushover.

98
00:10:58,750 --> 00:10:59,875
What's so funny?

99
00:11:01,916 --> 00:11:02,916
You.

100
00:11:04,333 --> 00:11:06,125
How little you know about women.

101
00:11:06,208 --> 00:11:09,000
It's easy to see she's the wild one.

102
00:11:09,083 --> 00:11:11,041
You're the tame one. The pushover.

103
00:11:11,125 --> 00:11:13,041
- Shut up.
- You can't handle her.

104
00:11:13,125 --> 00:11:16,291
For a woman like her,
a dozen of you wouldn’t cut it.

105
00:11:16,375 --> 00:11:18,083
Shut up, goddammit.

106
00:11:19,208 --> 00:11:21,041
Two months in, they despise you.

107
00:11:21,125 --> 00:11:24,166
Didn't you hear me?
I said shut the fuck up!

108
00:11:24,250 --> 00:11:28,416
Oh, you think you’re tough now?
Why don't you try that on her?

109
00:11:29,291 --> 00:11:30,791
You're a weakling.

110
00:11:30,875 --> 00:11:35,291
Look who had the last word.
You just stood there looking stupid.

111
00:11:35,375 --> 00:11:37,875
Do what you gotta do, dammit! Come on!

112
00:11:52,666 --> 00:11:53,833
We're here.

113
00:12:17,958 --> 00:12:19,208
Let's do it.

114
00:12:48,333 --> 00:12:50,583
Looks like it's over 100 feet deep.

115
00:12:51,083 --> 00:12:54,166
The duke didn't exactly roll out
the red carpet for us.

116
00:13:52,375 --> 00:13:54,291
- Clear.
- Clear.

117
00:13:55,083 --> 00:13:56,333
All clear. Come down.

118
00:14:07,541 --> 00:14:08,916
Bruce, you okay?

119
00:14:09,666 --> 00:14:11,250
Are you stuck?

120
00:14:19,375 --> 00:14:20,916
<i>Bruce, why'd you stop?</i>

121
00:14:24,916 --> 00:14:26,875
What kind of sexual contact?

122
00:14:26,958 --> 00:14:28,791
Bruce, this isn't the time.

123
00:14:28,875 --> 00:14:31,208
So, in the truck,
it was the time, but not now?

124
00:14:31,291 --> 00:14:33,541
You decide when it's okay?

125
00:14:33,625 --> 00:14:34,875
Keila, all okay?

126
00:14:34,958 --> 00:14:37,250
Where did it happen? In our bed?

127
00:14:37,333 --> 00:14:39,166
- No.
- Did you sleep together?

128
00:14:39,250 --> 00:14:41,083
No, we didn't sleep.

129
00:14:41,166 --> 00:14:42,583
Did you orgasm?

130
00:14:42,666 --> 00:14:44,541
<i>Bruce, please stop.</i>

131
00:14:45,708 --> 00:14:47,000
So you did.

132
00:14:48,291 --> 00:14:49,625
Did you like it better?

133
00:14:52,041 --> 00:14:53,208
<i>Bruce, Keila.</i>

134
00:14:53,291 --> 00:14:55,000
Come down immediately.

135
00:15:16,291 --> 00:15:17,750
That way.

136
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:20,375
We are 2,000 feet away from the cellar.

137
00:15:23,625 --> 00:15:25,958
<i>The alarm lasers could be anywhere.</i>

138
00:15:26,041 --> 00:15:29,583
- In the tunnel or in the cellar.
- How will we find out where they are?

139
00:15:29,666 --> 00:15:33,875
We'll use a dense medium. Smoke machines.

140
00:15:37,458 --> 00:15:39,500
Clear. Let's move.

141
00:16:11,833 --> 00:16:13,833
Lie to yourself as much as you want.

142
00:16:15,458 --> 00:16:17,916
You can believe
I forced you to be with me,

143
00:16:18,416 --> 00:16:20,291
but you loved me, Cameron.

144
00:16:30,333 --> 00:16:31,750
And I still love you.

145
00:16:41,375 --> 00:16:42,541
Berlin is right.

146
00:16:44,833 --> 00:16:49,666
Here we are in Spain's most gorgeous city,
wasting our time hating each other.

147
00:16:53,958 --> 00:16:57,708
When I could fix all of this
with one kiss, right here and now.

148
00:17:11,833 --> 00:17:13,791
Then we'd hold hands.

149
00:17:18,125 --> 00:17:19,916
And get off this boat.

150
00:17:25,333 --> 00:17:28,208
<i>And head out and go wild in the city.</i>

151
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:31,666
We'd lose ourselves
in Triana's oldest bars.

152
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,833
<i>All full of noise and people.</i>

153
00:17:40,791 --> 00:17:44,791
We'd have to get close to hear each other.
You like when I talk into your ear.

154
00:17:44,875 --> 00:17:46,708
<i>You used to say it tickles you.</i>

155
00:17:50,333 --> 00:17:53,416
<i>You, fearless as ever,</i>
<i>would break into a flamenco dance.</i>

156
00:17:58,833 --> 00:18:00,875
<i>Everyone would be watching you, rapt.</i>

157
00:18:02,208 --> 00:18:03,708
<i>Starting with me.</i>

158
00:18:05,791 --> 00:18:09,041
<i>I'd try to clap along,</i>
<i>but with no flair at all</i>

159
00:18:09,125 --> 00:18:10,791
<i>because I've got no rhythm.</i>

160
00:18:11,375 --> 00:18:13,416
Then we'd linger, kissing each other.

161
00:18:22,083 --> 00:18:23,875
<i>Motionless, in a sea of people.</i>

162
00:18:26,083 --> 00:18:30,625
We'd do all the silly tourist stuff
and feel like we were discovering it.

163
00:18:30,708 --> 00:18:33,333
<i>We'd go to the most expensive boutique</i>
<i>in town,</i>

164
00:18:33,416 --> 00:18:37,750
<i>where aristocrats buy clothes,</i>
<i>and dress up like them for a while.</i>

165
00:18:38,333 --> 00:18:40,458
And damn, we'd look so good.

166
00:18:42,916 --> 00:18:45,041
<i>We'd get in a horse-drawn carriage</i>

167
00:18:45,125 --> 00:18:47,833
<i>and go around Seville</i>
<i>for all the world to see.</i>

168
00:18:49,791 --> 00:18:53,791
<i>Finally, we'd spend the night</i>
<i>at the most luxurious hotel in town.</i>

169
00:18:54,958 --> 00:18:58,000
And I say "spend,"
because we wouldn't sleep at all.

170
00:19:22,333 --> 00:19:23,333
Cameron…

171
00:19:24,125 --> 00:19:25,125
What?

172
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,291
Was what happened that night so bad…

173
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:31,833
that it ruins any chance for us?

174
00:19:31,916 --> 00:19:33,333
It was you.

175
00:19:36,875 --> 00:19:38,375
It's your fault, Roi.

176
00:19:39,083 --> 00:19:41,458
It was you who pushed me over the edge.

177
00:19:41,541 --> 00:19:43,458
That's why it all fell apart that night.

178
00:19:44,583 --> 00:19:46,458
You always tried to change me.

179
00:19:47,458 --> 00:19:48,458
To save me.

180
00:19:51,708 --> 00:19:54,250
But all you've done
is screw me up even more.

181
00:19:57,458 --> 00:19:59,750
We can't pretend it didn't happen.

182
00:19:59,833 --> 00:20:00,833
Why?

183
00:20:01,666 --> 00:20:04,916
This is all a big mistake.
I shouldn't have come to Seville.

184
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,625
Cameron.

185
00:20:14,708 --> 00:20:18,250
- Tell Berlin I'm done. I can't be here.
- Cameron! For fuck's sake!

186
00:20:32,833 --> 00:20:34,375
I won't calm down, dammit!

187
00:21:11,083 --> 00:21:12,500
Last stop.

188
00:21:38,833 --> 00:21:40,916
The dome we spotted with the drone.

189
00:21:45,333 --> 00:21:46,333
Don't move.

190
00:21:49,416 --> 00:21:50,666
Not another step.

191
00:22:15,541 --> 00:22:17,416
It's like a laser cage.

192
00:22:17,500 --> 00:22:19,375
The collection's in there.

193
00:22:30,791 --> 00:22:33,041
It's odd. I'm not detecting cameras.

194
00:22:33,125 --> 00:22:36,208
They don't need any with this setup.

195
00:22:36,916 --> 00:22:40,125
<i>These lasers</i>
<i>work like any photoelectric cell.</i>

196
00:22:41,166 --> 00:22:44,916
Trip the laser, and you activate an alarm
or something worse.

197
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:46,458
Something worse?

198
00:22:46,541 --> 00:22:49,541
For an eccentric like our duke,
any twisted little trap.

199
00:22:49,625 --> 00:22:53,291
Like the floor opening up
and dropping us into a pit.

200
00:22:54,958 --> 00:22:55,958
Dead.

201
00:22:57,291 --> 00:22:59,416
Alive. Dead.

202
00:22:59,500 --> 00:23:01,541
Yeah, we get the idea.

203
00:23:01,625 --> 00:23:05,500
But how will we get past
the best security system in the world?

204
00:23:05,583 --> 00:23:11,000
His security system
was the best until a few years ago.

205
00:23:11,083 --> 00:23:12,625
Keila, go on.

206
00:23:12,708 --> 00:23:17,125
According to classified documents,
the duke installed the system in 2000,

207
00:23:17,208 --> 00:23:18,750
but it's now a bit obsolete.

208
00:23:18,833 --> 00:23:21,333
A weakness was found a few years ago.

209
00:23:21,416 --> 00:23:23,208
I made a video to show you.

210
00:23:23,291 --> 00:23:26,291
The laser has a two-degree tolerance
at the entry point.

211
00:23:26,375 --> 00:23:28,958
Enough for us to fool the alarm.

212
00:23:29,041 --> 00:23:30,125
How?

213
00:23:30,208 --> 00:23:34,625
We'll swap their laser beam with our own.
Same frequency, power, and size.

214
00:23:34,708 --> 00:23:38,000
Once we fit our laser
in that extra space in the receiver,

215
00:23:38,083 --> 00:23:40,250
we cover the emitter and make an opening.

216
00:23:40,333 --> 00:23:45,583
How will we know
the right power, frequency, and size?

217
00:23:46,833 --> 00:23:49,083
The smoke will let us see
the beam's diameter.

218
00:23:49,166 --> 00:23:52,666
We'll just have to analyze the frequency
with a spectrometer.

219
00:23:59,166 --> 00:24:00,041
Two millimeters.

220
00:24:06,833 --> 00:24:09,791
<i>And once we have the laser</i>
<i>with the exact size,</i>

221
00:24:09,875 --> 00:24:14,333
how will we overlay it on the system
with a two-degree variation?

222
00:24:14,416 --> 00:24:16,666
No human hand is that precise.

223
00:24:16,750 --> 00:24:18,916
Exactly, no human hand.

224
00:24:19,625 --> 00:24:22,541
We'll use neurosurgery robotic arms.

225
00:24:22,625 --> 00:24:25,958
We'll be able to set the laser
in the exact point of the spectrum,

226
00:24:26,041 --> 00:24:27,708
without even a 1-degree variance.

227
00:24:49,875 --> 00:24:51,500
Berlin, scan the space.

228
00:25:12,416 --> 00:25:15,833
We need to move the robotic arms
432.6 millimeters

229
00:25:15,916 --> 00:25:17,333
to coincide with the lasers.

230
00:25:17,416 --> 00:25:20,750
With an exact angle of 91.36 degrees.

231
00:25:20,833 --> 00:25:22,166
Set the laser pointers.

232
00:25:31,083 --> 00:25:31,916
Here we go.

233
00:26:11,291 --> 00:26:14,791
I've seen faster robots.
C-3PO would run circles around this gizmo.

234
00:26:14,875 --> 00:26:17,625
I need to make sure
the parameters are correct.

235
00:26:17,708 --> 00:26:21,125
- This level of precision takes time.
- Fine. I'll shut up.

236
00:26:21,833 --> 00:26:24,666
Look at this bastard's setup.

237
00:26:26,333 --> 00:26:29,500
The wine barrels, the albero sand floors…

238
00:26:30,291 --> 00:26:34,791
Nobody sets all this up
unless they're hiding something huge.

239
00:26:48,500 --> 00:26:50,375
It's the moment of truth.

240
00:26:50,875 --> 00:26:53,625
We'll block the real alarm lasers.

241
00:27:15,833 --> 00:27:17,666
I think we fooled the system.

242
00:27:19,875 --> 00:27:21,375
Your girlfriend's a pro.

243
00:27:25,166 --> 00:27:27,666
There's our way in.

244
00:28:43,125 --> 00:28:44,583
Shit.

245
00:28:57,833 --> 00:29:00,666
Come on. Fuck.

246
00:29:01,833 --> 00:29:04,791
<i>The number you called is switched off</i>
<i>or unavailable.</i>

247
00:29:04,875 --> 00:29:06,708
<i>Leave a message after the tone.</i>

248
00:29:08,083 --> 00:29:11,583
Damián, I hope you get this in time.
The guard escaped.

249
00:29:14,958 --> 00:29:17,083
I was on deck.
He can't have left the boat.

250
00:29:20,166 --> 00:29:22,541
I'll get far from land so he can't escape.

251
00:29:25,250 --> 00:29:29,291
Damián, if that fucker
manages to warn the duke, you're dead.

252
00:29:39,333 --> 00:29:42,125
You can go through
by lifting your leg carefully.

253
00:30:03,666 --> 00:30:05,375
Your shoelace is untied!

254
00:30:13,333 --> 00:30:14,791
Take your boots off.

255
00:30:16,375 --> 00:30:17,958
Okay, coming.

256
00:30:31,333 --> 00:30:35,375
I feel like a chump getting told
to take my shoes off at the airport.

257
00:30:35,458 --> 00:30:38,208
I once made the mistake
of flying commercial.

258
00:30:38,291 --> 00:30:41,000
They made me stick my feet
in tiny blue plastic bags

259
00:30:41,083 --> 00:30:43,083
to get through security.

260
00:30:44,291 --> 00:30:46,041
I've traveled by boat ever since.

261
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:51,333
And now, Keila, if you'll allow me…

262
00:31:00,125 --> 00:31:02,375
Ready for the big moment?

263
00:32:09,875 --> 00:32:13,541
<i>The Storm on the Sea of Galilee,</i>
by Rembrandt.

264
00:32:14,041 --> 00:32:15,791
The real one.

265
00:32:17,000 --> 00:32:21,708
Stolen from Boston's
Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum

266
00:32:21,791 --> 00:32:23,250
23 years ago.

267
00:32:36,583 --> 00:32:38,291
<i>Poppy Flowers,</i>

268
00:32:40,666 --> 00:32:42,083
by Van Gogh.

269
00:32:45,125 --> 00:32:48,041
This one was stolen twice
from the Cairo Museum.

270
00:32:50,958 --> 00:32:55,833
<i>View of Auvers-sur-Oise.</i>

271
00:32:58,750 --> 00:33:00,125
Cézanne.

272
00:33:04,000 --> 00:33:08,166
<i>Woman with a Fan, </i>Amedeo Modigliani.

273
00:33:08,250 --> 00:33:11,625
This was stolen from Paris's
Museum of Modern Art.

274
00:33:18,833 --> 00:33:20,500
The <i>Nativity,</i>

275
00:33:23,250 --> 00:33:24,708
by Caravaggio.

276
00:33:26,875 --> 00:33:30,916
The most valuable stolen painting
in all of art history.

277
00:33:36,291 --> 00:33:39,500
And he has them here, in his cellar.

278
00:33:41,291 --> 00:33:43,083
As one keeps bottles of port.

279
00:33:51,083 --> 00:33:54,000
What's with him? Is he having a breakdown?

280
00:33:55,000 --> 00:33:58,333
- Big-time Stendhal episode.
- What?

281
00:34:02,875 --> 00:34:04,625
Stendhal syndrome.

282
00:34:04,708 --> 00:34:08,041
Euphoria causing palpitations,
happiness, and fascination

283
00:34:08,125 --> 00:34:10,041
when contemplating beauty.

284
00:34:10,125 --> 00:34:14,250
We'll admire it all tomorrow.
I don't want to stay here much longer.

285
00:34:14,333 --> 00:34:16,958
We cut the canvases off
and leave the frames, right?

286
00:34:18,125 --> 00:34:22,041
What are you doing, you fool?

287
00:34:27,916 --> 00:34:30,166
You want to take them in the frames?

288
00:34:30,250 --> 00:34:33,583
Of course not, Damián.

289
00:34:35,791 --> 00:34:38,208
Because we're not taking them.

290
00:34:45,500 --> 00:34:48,041
What do you mean?

291
00:34:48,125 --> 00:34:53,833
These are not an empress's necklaces
or a cache of unmarked bills.

292
00:34:53,916 --> 00:34:59,041
Before you are the greatest stolen works
in history.

293
00:34:59,125 --> 00:35:05,208
The world's most mysterious
and coveted paintings.

294
00:35:05,291 --> 00:35:07,500
But that contemptible,

295
00:35:08,541 --> 00:35:14,583
egomaniacal narcissist
has them here, sequestered.

296
00:35:14,666 --> 00:35:17,458
There are millions of paintings
around the world.

297
00:35:17,541 --> 00:35:20,083
If people can't see these,
they will go see others.

298
00:35:21,083 --> 00:35:22,333
Come, please.

299
00:35:25,250 --> 00:35:28,166
Do you know how many times
I've visited the Uffizi Gallery

300
00:35:28,250 --> 00:35:30,958
to bask in the presence
of <i>The Birth of Venus?</i>

301
00:35:32,916 --> 00:35:37,875
Every time I am depressed
and lose faith in human nature.

302
00:35:37,958 --> 00:35:41,250
And do you know
why I go there time and time again?

303
00:35:43,583 --> 00:35:48,708
Because when I gaze upon that piece,

304
00:35:49,916 --> 00:35:51,916
I regain my calm.

305
00:35:52,416 --> 00:35:55,625
What is art, Bruce?

306
00:36:02,166 --> 00:36:07,208
The highest vibration of the human soul.

307
00:36:08,541 --> 00:36:10,541
Each one of these paintings

308
00:36:10,625 --> 00:36:14,041
was created to reconcile
the human soul with the beauty

309
00:36:15,208 --> 00:36:16,791
and pain of the world.

310
00:36:17,291 --> 00:36:19,583
But this duke is so arrogant

311
00:36:20,666 --> 00:36:24,833
that he had to set up this bordello here
with its stolen art,

312
00:36:25,333 --> 00:36:29,291
its wine, its bed, and even its landline
to cheat his own inhibitors

313
00:36:29,375 --> 00:36:31,708
and have his dinner
brought to his chamber.

314
00:36:31,791 --> 00:36:33,041
It's repugnant.

315
00:36:33,125 --> 00:36:35,291
So then what do we do?

316
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:39,500
Give me three minutes. I need to think.

317
00:36:39,583 --> 00:36:44,000
Is this the right place to do that?
He could be watching us!

318
00:36:44,583 --> 00:36:47,500
Don't worry. There aren't any cameras.

319
00:36:47,583 --> 00:36:51,916
What if there's sonar or a detector?
And if he already knows we're here?

320
00:39:39,875 --> 00:39:44,416
Look at the marks on my face
because I'm going to ask you a question.

321
00:39:44,916 --> 00:39:46,083
Look at me!

322
00:39:47,833 --> 00:39:48,833
Tell me.

323
00:39:50,583 --> 00:39:51,708
Do you like dogs?

324
00:39:54,125 --> 00:39:57,125
There are only two answers, yes or no.

325
00:39:57,625 --> 00:39:58,833
Yes or no?

326
00:39:58,916 --> 00:40:00,875
Yes.

327
00:40:02,000 --> 00:40:03,250
Then bark.

328
00:40:04,208 --> 00:40:06,208
Bark, dammit! Bark!

329
00:40:06,708 --> 00:40:08,041
- Bark!
- Woof!

330
00:40:08,125 --> 00:40:09,750
- More!
- Woof!

331
00:40:11,916 --> 00:40:13,208
Good boy.

332
00:40:29,083 --> 00:40:31,208
That's it. It's been three minutes.

333
00:40:35,041 --> 00:40:37,041
Put that painting down right now.

334
00:40:37,125 --> 00:40:39,916
What are you going to do?
Point a gun at me?

335
00:40:40,708 --> 00:40:41,958
I won't.

336
00:40:42,041 --> 00:40:44,416
You forced the gang
to pick your plan over mine,

337
00:40:44,500 --> 00:40:46,833
because robbing deposit boxes was madness.

338
00:40:46,916 --> 00:40:49,250
You convinced them and humiliated me.

339
00:40:49,333 --> 00:40:52,916
Now in this laser cage,
you decide we're not stealing these?

340
00:40:53,708 --> 00:40:55,041
We're robbing this place.

341
00:40:55,125 --> 00:40:57,750
We sure as hell are.

342
00:40:57,833 --> 00:41:00,458
That Monet is coming with me,

343
00:41:00,541 --> 00:41:03,000
even if I can only hang it
in my office at school.

344
00:41:03,083 --> 00:41:04,875
Hang on.

345
00:41:10,416 --> 00:41:11,916
You're completely right.

346
00:41:15,333 --> 00:41:17,541
But I just had an epiphany.

347
00:41:18,916 --> 00:41:20,583
And I've seen things clearly.

348
00:41:22,000 --> 00:41:24,041
These works of art, these pieces,

349
00:41:24,125 --> 00:41:29,291
will be the key to the biggest
and most poetic heist in history.

350
00:41:29,791 --> 00:41:31,041
And we'll do it together.

351
00:41:31,916 --> 00:41:32,958
You and I.

352
00:41:33,708 --> 00:41:36,666
I'm asking you, for everything
you hold sacred, trust me.

353
00:41:47,750 --> 00:41:52,166
Keila, can you hide this landline's number
if I make a call?

354
00:41:52,250 --> 00:41:53,500
Yes, of course I can.

355
00:41:54,208 --> 00:41:55,208
Do it.

356
00:42:08,083 --> 00:42:11,541
You told me to put on the clothes
laid out on the bed.

357
00:42:11,625 --> 00:42:14,208
I've been waiting for 40 minutes.

358
00:42:14,291 --> 00:42:17,208
I was on the porch,
seeing off our guests, love.

359
00:42:17,291 --> 00:42:18,291
Right.

360
00:42:29,750 --> 00:42:30,750
Come.

361
00:42:32,208 --> 00:42:33,208
Come.

362
00:42:40,625 --> 00:42:44,041
My toreador jacket fits you like a glove.

363
00:42:45,791 --> 00:42:48,208
I hope this is not my birthday present.

364
00:42:49,916 --> 00:42:53,333
Because… I'm not so sure I like it.

365
00:42:53,416 --> 00:42:54,416
No.

366
00:42:55,708 --> 00:42:58,500
This is just a little whim of mine.

367
00:43:00,500 --> 00:43:02,083
Your present's here.

368
00:43:14,458 --> 00:43:15,958
Piñatas?

369
00:43:24,416 --> 00:43:28,500
Nothing like the eager excitement
of our childhood birthday parties.

370
00:43:29,708 --> 00:43:32,041
I love children's games.

371
00:43:59,500 --> 00:44:01,250
You can only break two piñatas.

372
00:44:02,458 --> 00:44:04,583
Choose well, my love.

373
00:44:34,125 --> 00:44:35,125
Hello?

374
00:44:35,208 --> 00:44:37,250
<i>Good evening, Duke. It's Berlin.</i>

375
00:44:39,250 --> 00:44:41,166
Forgive me for calling this late,

376
00:44:41,250 --> 00:44:45,583
but I believe there's something important
that you and I should discuss.

377
00:44:45,666 --> 00:44:47,625
At this hour? Can't it wait?

378
00:44:47,708 --> 00:44:48,875
<i>Let's say it can't.</i>

379
00:44:48,958 --> 00:44:51,750
I think it's best
if we get together tonight.

380
00:44:52,458 --> 00:44:55,500
I'm with my team,
and I'd like you to meet them.

381
00:44:55,583 --> 00:44:58,333
<i>You see, I'm nearby, on your estate.</i>

382
00:44:58,416 --> 00:45:00,541
<i>Inside your art gallery, to be precise.</i>

383
00:45:00,625 --> 00:45:01,916
My art gallery?

384
00:45:02,000 --> 00:45:03,416
We'll be waiting here.

385
00:45:04,291 --> 00:45:05,500
<i>I'll go right away.</i>

386
00:45:11,541 --> 00:45:12,666
You're really leaving?

387
00:45:14,208 --> 00:45:15,541
But I'm your wife.

388
00:45:17,750 --> 00:45:18,750
Álvaro.

389
00:45:20,750 --> 00:45:23,708
I think you're more
into your collection than into me.

390
00:45:24,666 --> 00:45:26,250
I'll be right back, darling.

391
00:45:27,458 --> 00:45:29,666
Don't take that off. You look beautiful.

392
00:46:16,541 --> 00:46:17,750
Let me out, you bastard!

393
00:46:17,833 --> 00:46:20,708
I put you in there with my lame doggie.

394
00:46:21,208 --> 00:46:22,958
Her fate was sealed.

395
00:46:23,458 --> 00:46:26,333
Let me out of here, you son of a bitch!

396
00:46:27,833 --> 00:46:30,458
Give me that finger. Here.

397
00:46:31,833 --> 00:46:33,416
Let go.

398
00:46:35,041 --> 00:46:36,916
Don't move. That's it.

399
00:46:39,958 --> 00:46:43,791
You've been good dogs.
I'm putting you out of your misery.

400
00:46:45,291 --> 00:46:46,958
No!

401
00:46:47,041 --> 00:46:48,583
No, please!

402
00:46:49,083 --> 00:46:50,750
No!

403
00:46:53,125 --> 00:46:54,291
No, please!

404
00:46:55,000 --> 00:46:55,916
No!

405
00:49:36,625 --> 00:49:38,541
Subtitle translation by:
Soledad Etchemendy

